/**
 * @defgroup BtofGeo BtofGeo — Barrel Time-of-Flight Geometry
 * @ingroup StarVMCGeometry
 * @brief AGML geometry definition for the STAR Barrel Time-of-Flight (BTOF) detector.
 *
 * @details
 * The BTOF detector surrounds the STAR TPC at radii 207.8–221.0 cm and covers
 * |η| < 0.9 over 2π in azimuth.  It provides particle identification via
 * time-of-flight measurement, enabling π/K/p separation up to ~1.6 GeV/c
 * (π/K) and ~3 GeV/c (K/p).  The final system consists of 120 trays (60 west,
 * 60 east), each containing 32 MRPC strips.  Earlier configurations reused the
 * same tray slots for the Central Trigger Barrel (CTB) plastic-scintillator slabs
 * and for TOFp/TOFr prototype modules.  Run 13 introduced GEM-based trays at two
 * positions per half.
 *
 * The geometry is selected via the `btog.choice` parameter and, for full-system
 * runs, the `btog.posit5[120]` per-tray activation map.  The BtofConfig.xml
 * registry provides 14 named setups spanning every experimental era.
 *
 * @{
 */

/**
 * @defgroup BtofGeo1 BtofGeo1 — CTB + 1-tray TOFp (legacy)
 * @ingroup BtofGeo
 * @brief Module @c BTOFGEO1: Central Trigger Barrel geometry with optional single
 *        TOFp prototype tray.
 *
 * @details
 * Implements the original CTB plastic-scintillator slabs (BXSA active slabs
 * inside BMTC cavities) and the first TOFp prototype (BCSB slabs in BTTC
 * cavities).  Tray positions for the TOFp tray are set by `btog.posit1`.
 *
 * Structures: BTOG (envelope), TRAY (tray dims), CTBB (CTB slab dims),
 * TOFF (TOFp slat dims with individual per-slat z-positions Slat01z…Slat10z).
 *
 * Key volumes: BTOF → BTOH → BSEC → BTRA → BXTR → BMTC/BTTC → BMTD/BASS →
 * BXSA/BCSB + BCPM + BCSK/BTSK.
 *
 * Used by setups: @c BTOFof (off), @c BTOF42 (choice=4, single TOFp tray).
 */

/**
 * @defgroup BtofGeo2 BtofGeo2 — CTB + TOFp + TOFr prototypes (Run 2–4)
 * @ingroup BtofGeo
 * @brief Module @c BTOFGEO2: Adds Run-3/4 TOFr MRPC prototype (BRTC cavity).
 *
 * @details
 * Extends BtofGeo1 with the TOFr prototype MRPC module geometry.  Adds
 * structures MODR (Run-3 MRPC dims) and MOD4 (Run-4 MRPC dims).  The BGMT
 * gas-box volume replaces the full honeycomb structure to model the slimmer
 * MRPC tray.  The BRFE volume models the TOFr front-end electronics board.
 *
 * Structures: BTOG (+ posit2), TRAY, CTBB, TOFF (Slat01z…Slat10z), MODR, MOD4.
 *
 * Used by setups: @c BTOF42 (choice=4), @c BTOF52 (choice=5), @c BTOF72 (choice=7).
 */

/**
 * @defgroup BtofGeo3 BtofGeo3 — CTB + multi-prototype refinement
 * @ingroup BtofGeo
 * @brief Module @c BTOFGEO3: Geometry refinements over BtofGeo2; same structural
 *        schema and volume set.
 *
 * @details
 * Structural layout is identical to BtofGeo2.  Updated numerical values in the
 * Fill tables reflect measured as-built dimensions from early prototype runs.
 * Still uses the TOFF slat-z array (Slat01z…Slat10z).
 */

/**
 * @defgroup BtofGeo4 BtofGeo4 — Run-5/6/7 prototype configuration
 * @ingroup BtofGeo
 * @brief Module @c BTOFGEO4: Adds @c posit3 tray slot for Run-5/6/7 prototype.
 *
 * @details
 * Adds `btog.posit3` (a single tray number) to select the Run-5/6/7 TOFr
 * prototype position.  Otherwise structurally identical to BtofGeo2/3.
 *
 * Used by setup: @c BTOF84 (choice=8).
 */

/**
 * @defgroup BtofGeo5 BtofGeo5 — Extended prototype with array MRPC dims
 * @ingroup BtofGeo
 * @brief Module @c BTOFGEO5: Replaces per-slat z-arrays with MODR containing
 *        per-strip (mrpcX, mrpcZ, mrpcA) position arrays; adds backplane
 *        geometry.
 *
 * @details
 * The TOFF structure now holds `Slatz(10)`, `Slatx(10)`, `SlatAy(10)`, and
 * `Elecz(10)` arrays.  The MODR structure provides `mrpcX(33)`, `mrpcZ(33)`,
 * `mrpcA(33)` for 33 strip positions per tray.  Additional backplane connector
 * volumes (BLEM) and cooling pipe (BPIP) are introduced.  Adds `posit4(5)` for
 * five additional prototype tray positions.
 *
 * Used by setup: @c BTOFa5 (choice=10).
 */

/**
 * @defgroup BtofGeo6 BtofGeo6 — Full MRPC system, Run 8 and later (v6)
 * @ingroup BtofGeo
 * @brief Module @c BTOFGEO6: Complete 120-tray MRPC system with per-tray
 *        activation map @c posit5[120] and global offsets @c X0, @c Z0.
 *
 * @details
 * Introduces the full Run-8 tray layout.  The BTOG structure gains `X0`
 * (radial offset), `Z0` (z edge offset), `posit5(120)` (per-tray
 * install/empty flag), and `dphi1(5)` (phi alignment corrections for five
 * east/west boundary trays).  The TRAY structure gains top cover and FEE
 * bracket dimensions (TopThk, TopH, CoverThk, CoverH, CoverL, FEEH1, FEEH2,
 * FEEW, FEEL, FEEThk).  New blocks: BTFE (TINO/TDIG boards), BCON (generic
 * connector/foam block), BFEE (FEE G10 board), BLEM (Lemo connector).
 *
 * Used by setups: @c BTOF16 (choice=1, z0=−0.50), @c BTOF66 (choice=6),
 * @c BTOFb6 (choice=11, z0=−0.50), @c BTOFc6 (choice=12).
 */

/**
 * @defgroup BtofGeo7 BtofGeo7 — Full MRPC system, Run 8 and later (v7)
 * @ingroup BtofGeo
 * @brief Module @c BTOFGEO7: Parallel full-system geometry identical to
 *        BtofGeo6 with independent version bookkeeping.
 *
 * @details
 * Structurally and volumetrically identical to BtofGeo6.  Maintained as a
 * separate module to allow independent versioning in simulation production.
 *
 * Used by setups: @c BTOF67, @c BTOFb7, @c BTOFc7.
 */

/**
 * @defgroup BtofGeo8 BtofGeo8 — Full MRPC + GEM trays (Run 13+)
 * @ingroup BtofGeo
 * @brief Module @c BtofGeo8: Adds @c posit13[120] tray-type map and the
 *        @c GMTR structure for GEM-readout trays installed from Run 13.
 *
 * @details
 * Extends BtofGeo6/7 with the GMTR parameter structure, which encodes all
 * dimensions of the GEM-based tray inserts: inner frame (GINW, GINL, GINThk),
 * NF foam pieces (GNFThk, GNFL, GNFW), support boards (GSB*), GEM foils
 * (GEML, GEMW, GEMThk, GEMGThk and layer thicknesses GEMThka–d), APV
 * front-end chips (APVL, APVW, APVThk), HV distribution boards (HVThk,
 * HVW, HVL), vacuum connectors (GVI, GVO, GVL, GCL, GCI, GCO), and
 * additional positional parameters (POS1[3], POS2[3]).
 *
 * The `posit13[120]` array assigns each tray a type: 7 = standard MRPC tray,
 * 8 = GEM tray.  In Run 13 trays 8 and 23 (west) and 92 and 108 (east) are
 * GEM trays.
 *
 * Used by setup: @c BTOFv8 (choice=13).
 */

/**
 * @}
 */
